palette.json
  Derived from the outlines of both imports above — it is the graph colouring
  of who borders whom, over every shard at once — and so it carries both their
  licences, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 and GPL-3.0-only together, and not data/LICENSE.
  It cannot be split the way the shards can: one colouring answers the whole
  span, and an actor's hue is chosen against neighbours from either source.
  It holds no geometry and no coordinate: one small integer per actor,
  saying which of the eight hues the map draws that actor's territory in.
  Regeneration is reproducible with tools/build-palette.mjs.

Any geometry later imported from another source gets its own directory, its
own paragraph here and its own attribution in the interface. Imported
geometry is never merged into record files (see ARCHITECTURE.md).
